phi-adapter-sdk (0.10.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * HTTP authentication, in phi/adapter/net/http_auth.h: reading a
    WWW-Authenticate challenge and answering it with Digest MD5 (qop=auth,
    MD5-sess, and the older RFC 2069 form) or Basic. What
    QNetworkAccessManager did for the adapters without anyone writing a line
    of it, and the piece the FRITZ!Box adapter cannot leave Qt without - a
    FRITZ!Box answers TR-064 with Digest MD5 and nothing else.
  * Pure: a header string in, a header string out. Both worked examples the
    RFCs print - RFC 2617 section 3.5 and RFC 7616 section 3.9.1 - are
    reproduced byte for byte in the tests, so the arithmetic is checked
    against somebody else's answer rather than against itself.
  * phi/adapter/net/http_message.h: HTTP/1.1 framing, incremental, so a
    response arriving in whatever pieces the network chose is read correctly -
    Content-Length, chunked, and the older form framed only by the close.
  * phi/adapter/net/http_client.h: one request at a time on a phi::runtime
    loop, with the challenge round trip handled inside and the answer kept, so
    it happens once per device rather than once per request. The Qt-free
    replacement for QNetworkAccessManager plus a nested QEventLoop - and the
    nested loop is the part worth losing: it dispatched every queued callback,
    so any adapter callback could run inside any other.
  * `https://` is refused with a plain message rather than half-built. Nothing
    that has left Qt needs it yet.
  * Builds against libssl-dev for MD5.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Mon, 08 Sep 2026 11:35:00 +0200

